      "cluster_id": 5,
      "headline_hint": "ISRO successfully launches Earth observation satellite EOS-05 into geosynchronous orbit",
      "section": "india",
      "batch_position": 0,
      "claim_count": 12,
      "distinct_outlets": 3,
      "source_kinds": {
        "fulltext": 12
      },
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": 59,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO) successfully launched the EOS-05 Earth observation satellite aboard a Geosynchronous Satellite Launch Vehicle (GSLV) on September 4.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/science/isro-gslv-f17-eos-05-satellite-rocket-launch-september-4-sriharikota-updates/article71425914.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The GSLV placed EOS-05 into a Sub-Geosynchronous Transfer Orbit 18 minutes after lifting off from Sriharikota at 2.55 a.m. on September 4.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/science/isro-gslv-f17-eos-05-satellite-rocket-launch-september-4-sriharikota-updates/article71425914.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "EOS-05 is India's first imaging satellite designed to monitor Earth from a geosynchronous orbit approximately 36,000 km high.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/science/isro-gslv-f17-eos-05-satellite-rocket-launch-september-4-sriharikota-updates/article71425914.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "ISRO Chairman Dr. V. Narayanan stated that EOS-05 is the heaviest satellite ever launched by a GSLV rocket, weighing 2,367 kg.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/science/isro-gslv-f17-eos-05-satellite-rocket-launch-september-4-sriharikota-updates/article71425914.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "EOS-05 replaces the EOS-03 mission, which failed in August 2021 due to a cryogenic upper stage ignition anomaly.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/science/isro-gslv-f17-eos-05-satellite-rocket-launch-september-4-sriharikota-updates/article71425914.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "ISRO had not conducted any launch missions since the failure of the PSLV-C62 mission on January 12, 2026.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/science/isro-gslv-f17-eos-05-satellite-rocket-launch-september-4-sriharikota-updates/article71425914.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The GSLV-F17 rocket is 51.7 metres tall and has a liftoff mass of 420.5 tonnes.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/isros-gslv-f17-successfully-places-eos-05-earth-observation-satellite-in-geosynchronous-orbit/articleshow/133746002.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "ISRO Chairman V. Narayanan announced that ISRO plans six more launches in the current financial year, including navigation satellite NVS-03 and the first uncrewed Gaganyaan mission.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/isros-gslv-f17-successfully-places-eos-05-earth-observation-satellite-in-geosynchronous-orbit/articleshow/133746002.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "India had 21 operational Earth observation satellites as of February 2026.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/isros-gslv-f17-successfully-places-eos-05-earth-observation-satellite-in-geosynchronous-orbit/articleshow/133746002.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The GSLV-F17 rocket lifted off following a 27.5-hour countdown from the Satish Dhawan Space Centre in Sriharikota.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/isros-gslv-f17-carrying-eos-05-earth-observation-spacecraft-takes-off-from-sriharikota-101788470019068.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The EOS-05 satellite is also designated as Gisat-1A.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/defence/news/24x7-eye-on-china-pakistan-borders-why-eos-05-launch-on-naughty-boy-is-key-to-indias-security/articleshow/133739162.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "EOS-05 carries two multispectral imagers, including one with a spatial resolution of 42 metres per pixel.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/defence/news/24x7-eye-on-china-pakistan-borders-why-eos-05-launch-on-naughty-boy-is-key-to-indias-security/articleshow/133739162.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        }
      ]
    },
